# AUTO-GENERATED by Claude Code
# Purpose: pydantic-ai capability for competitive player data from start.gg: what a player
# picks (characters, stages), the sets two players played, tournaments and who entered them.
# Wraps ds.data.startgg / ds.data.raw.startgg. Test prompt: "get stats for Sparg0".
# Usage: add startgg_capability to an Agent's capabilities (wired up in ds.ai.agent).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rule this file exists to keep: NO RESULTS REACH THE AGENT. The data layer has winners,
# scores, seeds and placements; the user preps for opponents and doesn't want to be told how
# good they are. So here:
# - no tool returns a result field (models are result-free; tables pick their columns below),
# - no tool takes a result parameter (no filter by winner, seed or placement),
# - ds.data.startgg.results is never imported.
# tests/ds/ai/test_startgg_capability.py checks all three. Don't loosen it without the user
# asking; if they do, add a separate tool rather than widening these.
#
# NOTE: left out on purpose, to revisit once we know what else start.gg data is good for:
# - get_head_to_head gives no sets-won tally, score or winner, although
#   ds.data.startgg.head_to_head has them (`sets_won_1`, `score_1`, `winner`). A head-to-head
#   record is the obvious thing to ask for, so this is the first exception the user may want.
# - get_event_entrants gives no seeds or placements (`Entrant.seed`, `.placement`).
# - There is no results tool at all (ds.data.startgg.results.player_results is Python only).
# - TODO: no VOD tool: only ~1% of sets have a `vodUrl` (see the Site notes in
#   ds/data/raw/startgg/client.py, "Ideas for later"). Videos come from ds.ai.smashtube.
